hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16012","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Khuzai, he said, a man said, O Messenger of Allah, has Islam an end, he said: Whatever household, and he said in another place, he said: Yes, whatever household of the Arabs or the non-Arabs that Allah intends good for, He brings Islam into them, he said: Then what, he said: Then trials occur like shadows, he said: No, by Allah, if Allah wills, he said: Nay, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, then you will return therein as black serpents raised up, some of you striking the necks of others. And Sufyan recited to me, al-Zuhri said, black serpents raised up. Sufyan said, the black snake set up, meaning it rises."
"16013","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Khuzai, he said, a Bedouin said, O Messenger of Allah, has Islam an end, he said: Yes, whatever household of the Arabs or the non-Arabs that Allah, mighty and majestic, intends good for, He brings Islam into them, he said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Then trials occur like shadows, and the Bedouin said: No, O Messenger of Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nay, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will surely return therein as black serpents raised up, some of you striking the necks of others."
"16014","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said, al-Awzai narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Qays narrated to us, he said, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Kurz al-Khuzai, he said, a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Messenger of Allah, has this affair an end, he said: Yes, whomever Allah intends good for, of non-Arab or Arab, He brings it into them, then trials occur like shadows, you return therein as black serpents raised up, some of you striking the necks of others, and the best of people that day is a believer secluded in a mountain pass, fearing his Lord, blessed and exalted, and sparing the people his evil. My father said."
"16015","And Muhammad ibn Musab al-Qarqasani narrated to me the like of the hadith of Ibn al-Mughirah, except that he said, Kurz ibn Hubaysh al-Khuzai."
